# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Contact & partner forms — no env vars, no backend of ours at all.
#
# ContactForm.jsx and PartnerForm.jsx are plain HTML forms
# (action="https://formsubmit.co/contact@asbizdev.com", method="POST") —
# the browser posts directly to FormSubmit.co, which emails CONTACT_EMAIL
# (lib/constants/site.js) and auto-replies to the visitor. Anti-spam is
# FormSubmit's own `_honey` honeypot field, rendered by
# components/forms/HoneypotField.jsx.
#
# ⚠️ FormSubmit requires a one-time confirmation per domain: the first real
# submission from a given origin triggers a confirmation email to
# CONTACT_EMAIL — click the link in it to activate delivery from that
# domain, otherwise submissions from it fail silently on FormSubmit's end.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LinkedIn article ingestion (api/ingest-article.js, §24 — Articles & Insights).
# Server-side only, not prefixed VITE_ — never exposed to the browser bundle.
# Called by an n8n workflow (server-to-server, credential in n8n's own store)
# for every new LinkedIn post; /internal/add-article.html is a manual fallback
# only. The endpoint upserts straight into Supabase and the article is live
# immediately — no PR, no review step, no rebuild — so this token must never
# be pasted into a page a browser loads other than the fallback form, and
# that form's URL should be treated as a secret too.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Shared secret n8n's HTTP Request node must send as the `x-ingest-token` header.
INGEST_TOKEN=0000

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase — Articles & Insights backend (see docs/ARTICLES_SUPABASE.md).
# Architecture: LinkedIn → RSS bridge → n8n → Supabase → this site.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public project URL and anon key, from Supabase dashboard → Project Settings
# → API. Use the bare project URL (e.g. https://xxxx.supabase.co) — NOT the
# "/rest/v1" REST endpoint shown elsewhere in that page; supabase-js appends
# that path itself. Row Level Security restricts anon reads to
# status = 'published' only.
#
# Articles are fetched exclusively from Server Components (`lib/data/`,
# `app/sitemap.js`) — never from the browser — so these are plain server env
# vars, no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix needed. Must be set in the build/runtime
# environment (e.g. Vercel project settings), not just in a local `.env`.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Service-role key — bypasses RLS. Used ONLY by api/ingest-article.js (writes
# new articles) and scripts/migrate-articles-to-supabase.mjs (one-time
# migration of legacy static articles). Never exposed to the browser, never
# used by the build scripts above.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
